  "scientific_commentary": [
    {
      "item_id": "msg_05a58dbe5301b13d016ae50acd1238819187955a74c1f8294b",
      "phase": "commentary",
      "text": "The heat obstruction is now exact. For\n\\[\n\\psi=-\\cos x+\\varepsilon\\sin^6x\\cos y,\n\\]\nordinary heat initially increases \\(\\int\\det(D^2\\psi)^2\\) at \\(\\varepsilon=1/1000\\). This is an actual eight-mode field, and the energy is polyconvex.\n\nI’m preserving that failure alongside the attained-corrector construction. The latter must supply a real gradient perturbation, not just a moment inequality.\n",
      "capture_sha256": "41dbecbbc1a8cecd68b32ce6ddb5f7cdb444ece7162637ca1f60903bb13de030"
    },
    {
      "item_id": "msg_05a58dbe5301b13d016ae50dee09c08191b5efc8f2c5c76d02",
      "phase": "commentary",
      "text": "The attained variational principle passed exact replay, including a constructed gradient corrector and full finite-\\(\\varepsilon\\) energy polynomials. I also proved a quantitative extension: any strict ROC homogeneous quartic on symmetric \\(2\\times2\\) matrices can be extended to a globally ROC sextic on all \\(2\\times2\\) matrices. A strict actual Hessian violation would transfer to that extension.\n\nThe broader searches have found no admitted negative field. I’m checking the constants and preserving that distinction in the completed sources.\n",
      "capture_sha256": "304dc78a49f6977b91125ee5b212018a858ed042780d7770473c28634a30481e"
    },
    {
      "item_id": "msg_05a58dbe5301b13d016ae50f3f4958819181c0d423aa533583",
      "phase": "commentary",
      "text": "The broader searches still give no admitted separation. I’ve now completed the extension argument in the positive direction too: a quartic with a strong Hessian-QC bound has a globally QC extension\n\\[\nH(\\operatorname{sym}A)+\\nu(b-c)^2+\\mu|A|^6\n\\]\nwith an explicit bound on \\(\\mu\\).\n\nThe proof uses an actual Hodge decomposition and quantitative \\(L^4\\) control of its correction. I’m receiving a standalone QC control to verify the construction.\n",
      "capture_sha256": "53c70102cd1f376d7998066b8033528c326de32cba1d26a294255f555a94ff13"
    },
    {
      "item_id": "msg_05a58dbe5301b13d016ae510cab10c8191a55f5e5ad21ae005",
      "phase": "commentary",
      "text": "The full QC extension passed exact receipt. For the whole fifteen-dimensional Hessian-ROC quartic cone, the construction gives globally ROC polynomials \\(P_\\eta\\), with\n\\[\nH\\text{ Hessian-QC}\\iff P_\\eta\\text{ QC for every }\\eta>0.\n\\]\nStrict actual violations also transfer by explicit scaling.\n\nThe standalone control is globally QC and non-polyconvex. Its large sextic coefficient proves existence; the sharp boundary remains unresolved.\n",
      "capture_sha256": "53c70102cd1f376d7998066b8033528c326de32cba1d26a294255f555a94ff13"
    }
  ],
